'' fbc's OWN '-target x86_64-linux-android' predefines (docs/tiko-android FACTS, probed with #print):
'' __FB_ANDROID__, __FB_UNIX__, __FB_X86__, __FB_ASM__ "intel" and __FB_64BIT__ -- and NOT
'' __FB_LINUX__, nor tiko's TIKO_OS_LINUX: Android isn't GNU/Linux. tiko's own spellings are
'' TIKO_OS_ANDROID and TIKO_ARCH_X86_64.
'' TEST: cli
'' ARGS: --pp-only -target android-x86_64 tests/driver/src/android-predefines.bas
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 0
'' EXPECT-OUT: ANDROID
'' EXPECT-OUT: UNIX
'' EXPECT-OUT: X86
'' EXPECT-OUT: HAS64
'' EXPECT-OUT: OS_ANDROID
'' EXPECT-OUT: ARCH_X86_64
'' EXPECT-OUT: intel
'' EXPECT-NOT: LINUXDEF
'' EXPECT-NOT: OSLINUX
'' EXPECT-NOT: PCOS
'' EXPECT-NOT: WIN
